module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.ad_hoc_hardware_probe_produces_no_receipt

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data ad_hoc_hardware_probe_produces_no_receipt: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "ad_hoc_hardware_probe_produces_no_receipt" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a probe against hardware answers the deciding question and produces no typed observation, so the answer survives only as prose and may not be cited.** INVALID STATE: an attempt is made against a device, the device answers, a human reads the answer, and the run's OUTPUT IS CONSOLE TEXT rather than a receipt. THE DISTINGUISHING FACT IS NOT THAT SOMEBODY FORGOT TO WRITE IT DOWN. Preservation was never available to skip, because the probe's result was never a receipt in the first place -- there is no carrier the run could have committed, so the only artifact that could survive is a recollection, and a recollection is exactly what the corpus refuses as authority. The defect is in the probe's SHAPE, not in the diligence of whoever ran it. ",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN ONE (2026-08-29): an operator run against a held Mt. Collins unit observed that GET /redfish/v1 returned 404, that the firmware self-reported as `0.32`, and that the service roster was web/kvm/cd-media/hd-media/ssh with no Redfish service. `extdeps.ampere.mt_collins_product_brief.bmc` records that the raw producer output of that run WAS NOT PRESERVED, and therefore types the AMI MegaRAC identification as an EXPECTATION rather than an observation, with its own text forbidding any workflow from reading it as an observation, as a build-grain protocol fact, or as any kind of authority. That module is the corroborating evidence that the corpus already knew and could not act: it names the receipt that would settle the question, and no such receipt is authored. ",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN TWO (2026-09-06, found 2026-09-10): a credential rotation was attempted against the same controller and the REST path answered `attempt to set previous password` against a policy-conforming secret -- a DECIDED, semantic response proving the endpoint exists, parses the field, and applies a password-history policy to it. gunbc#10630 records the sentence and nothing else. A corpus-wide search for any /api/ user or password request shape returns none: the only rotation body committed anywhere is the Redfish PATCH in `gunbc.tools.bmc_onboard`, whose plans name srv3 and srv4 and which cannot be the call that answered, because a Redfish PATCH against a controller with no Redfish returns 404 rather than a password-policy error. So the request that produced the deciding refusal exists nowhere and cannot be reconstructed from the diff. ",

    "HARM, AND IT IS KEYED ON THE PROBE RATHER THAN ON WHAT HAPPENED AFTERWARDS. The cost is that a fact already obtained must be obtained AGAIN from the device, because the first attempt committed nothing that may be cited. For specimen one that cost was paid and the fact recovered: a second run on 2026-09-05 re-established the firmware identity and the Redfish absence, and `gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_access_observation` preserved it properly -- committed raw bytes, a verified digest, and five Redfish paths refused against a web root that answered 200 as the discriminating control. For specimen two the cost cannot be paid at all today: the request shape is nowhere and the controller answered no ARP from its own /24 on 2026-09-10, so it cannot be re-run until someone physically plugs the unit in. WHETHER RECOVERY IS AVAILABLE IS CONTINGENT -- it needs the hardware to still exist, still be reachable, and someone willing to make the trip -- so a row keyed on `the evidence was destroyed` would be keyed on the consequence and would MISS the recoverable instance entirely. The class is the probe shape, and it fires in both. ",

    "AMENDED 2026-09-10, HOURS AFTER FILING, AND THE REASON IS ITSELF THE MECHANISM. As first written this row claimed the evidence for specimen one was destroyed and that every later lane must re-probe. That overstated the harm: the fact had already been recovered and preserved on 2026-09-05 by the very receipt the extdeps module specified. THE AUTHOR OF THIS ROW REACHED THE WRONG CONCLUSION BY READING `extdeps.ampere.mt_collins_product_brief.bmc` -- which correctly declines to be the authority for an observation outside its layer, and whose sentence that no receipt is authored WAS TRUE WHEN WRITTEN -- as though it were a census of the corpus. It was superseded eight days later by the receipt it named. A module declining authority for something outside its layer is not evidence about what the corpus holds. Recorded here rather than quietly fixed because a failure-mode ledger whose own entries overstate their harm teaches the next reader to discount it, which is the one thing a ledger cannot afford. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: this is NOT `production_actuation_unmodeled_beside_a_modeled_probe` -- there is no modeled probe standing beside the ad-hoc one, which is the point; and it is NOT a documentation lapse, because no amount of note-taking discipline produces a citable observation from a run whose output has no carrier. Recognition rule: for any question about an external device that a workflow must later CITE, ask what artifact the probe COMMITS. If the answer is console output, a chat message, or a sentence in a pull request body, the fact is already lost at the moment it is learned, however carefully it is transcribed. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, by re-probing the device -- which presupposes the device is reachable and is therefore not always available. CEILING: structurally guaranteed for the class of facts a modeled operation can carry, because a probe whose result is a typed observation by construction cannot produce an uncitable answer; it either yields the carrier or refuses. It is NOT structurally impossible: nothing prevents a human opening a terminal beside the modeled path, and the modeled path cannot forbid that. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: an intake operation that performs device identification and returns a typed observation -- Manager payload, service roster, and whether the Redfish service root answers -- committed as an intake receipt keyed to unit, attempt, endpoint and time, such that the identity is a PRODUCT of the trip rather than a premise of it. The receipt must be shaped so that EITHER answer lands cleanly, because a probe designed around the expected firmware is how the unpreserved run became de-facto authority in the first place. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
